# PROJECT CONTINUITY - SESSION MANAGEMENT PROTOCOL

## PURPOSE
For large, multi-phase projects that span many sessions, this rule ensures context is never lost between conversations.

## SESSION START (MANDATORY)
At the START of every session, before doing ANY work:
1. Read `CLAUDE.md` in the project root - understand current phase, active task, and decisions
2. Read `docs/PROGRESS.md` - know exactly what's been completed and what's next
3. Read `docs/DECISIONS.md` if making architectural choices - check if the decision was already made
4. Read `docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md` if working on anything that touches external services, APIs, deployment, or env vars - this is the single source of truth for all service configs, credentials locations, and setup status
5. Acknowledge to the user: briefly state what phase we're in and what we're working on

## BEFORE CODING ANY FEATURE
Before writing code for any feature or task:
1. Read the relevant `.claude/*.mdc` standards files for that task:
   - Building ANY UI → invoke /frontend-design skill FIRST, then read relevant .mdc files below
   - Building web UI → read `master-web-design-prompt.mdc`, `09-design-system.mdc`, `06-mobile-responsive-design.mdc`
   - Building mobile UI → read `33-mobile-app-design.mdc`, `09-design-system.mdc`
   - Building API → read `13-api-design-standards.mdc`, `01-security-fortress.mdc`
   - Database work → read `14-database-design.mdc`
   - Authentication → read `01-security-fortress.mdc`
   - Internationalization → read `23-internationalization.mdc`
   - Testing → read `17-testing-strategy.mdc`
   - Deployment (web) → read `21-ci-cd-pipeline.mdc`
   - Deployment (app stores) → read `34-app-store-deployment.mdc`
   - Error handling → read `12-error-handling-ux.mdc`
   - Performance → read `18-performance-optimization.mdc`
   - Cross-platform code → read `32-cross-platform-development.mdc`
   - Mobile architecture → read `35-mobile-app-architecture.mdc`
   - Native device APIs → read `36-native-device-apis.mdc`
   - Real-time sync → read `37-real-time-sync.mdc`
2. Follow the standards defined in those files
3. Always follow `master-protocol.mdc` (it's always active)
4. Always follow `38-audit-ready-code.mdc` (it's always active - every line of code must pass third-party audits)

## GUIDED APPROACH
If the user does not code and Claude does all implementation, follow `16-guided-setup-assistance.mdc`:
- Break tasks into small steps
- Give ONE step at a time when the user needs to do something (run a command, create an account, etc.)
- Wait for confirmation before moving on
- Explain the "why" briefly
- If something fails, troubleshoot before continuing

## SESSION END (MANDATORY)
At the END of every work session:
1. Update `CLAUDE.md`:
   - Update "Current Status" section with current phase and active task
   - Update "What's Been Completed" checklist
   - Add any new decisions to the "Key Decisions" table
   - Update "Last Updated" date
2. Update `docs/PROGRESS.md`:
   - Check off completed items
   - Add notes about anything in-progress or blocked
3. Offer to commit changes to Git with a meaningful message
4. Tell the user what was accomplished and what's next

## CRITICAL RULES
- NEVER start coding without knowing current project state
- NEVER make architectural decisions that contradict `docs/DECISIONS.md`
- NEVER skip reading relevant standards files before a task
- ALWAYS follow security standards from `01-security-fortress.mdc` - no exceptions
- If unsure about user intent, ASK - don't assume
